// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-23 | Modified: 2022-12-25
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1202
// Description: Detects suspicious Splwow64.exe process without any command line parameters
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/sbousseaden/status/1429401053229891590?s=12
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_splwow64_cli_anomaly.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\splwow64.exe" and ProcessCommandLine endswith "splwow64.exe"
